  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only multiprofile with avgpool and PCA substantially outperforms single-profile RNA and transformer aggregation, with both higher accuracy and F1. The main uncertainty is whether a learned RNA encoder such as scvi_n200 improves over PCA under this same promising profile/aggregation setting. config_005 tests this by changing only the RNA encoder while keeping multiprofile and avgpool fixed, making it a clean one-factor comparison. It is the best next experiment because it exploits the current best RNA direction while reducing uncertainty about representation quality, rather than jumping to multimodal fusion where the image modality is currently weak and multiple factors would change at once."
}

